Pre-requisites
You need MSOL-SERVICE installed in powershell and be connected to MSOL-SERVICE in a powershell ISE session
Global Admin role account member

ForcePasswordResetAllUsers.ps1
Will only prompt all users to reset password at next logon

ForcePasswordResetAllUsersDefinedNewPassword.ps1
Will reset all users passwords to predefined ones you create

Get-MsolUser -All | Export-Csv "path to file name"

If using NewPassword ps1 you can add a column in your exported CSV named "NewPassword" and insert your own random password

Open either script in ISE enter "path to file name" and run it.

You may also run the last line of the script independently and change variable $upn to be a specific UPN for single user.